# Cursor Editor — Context Management

## Overview

Effective context management is the foundation of accurate AI-assisted development. Cursor provides multiple mechanisms for injecting project context into the agent's understanding, with `@`-symbol references being the primary interface.

---

## @-Symbol Reference System

Cursor uses `@`-symbols to include precise code context. Surgical references ensure the agent focuses on the right code.

### Reference Types

| Syntax | Type | Scope | Use Case |
|---|---|---|---|
| `@file <path>` | File context | Complete file | When entire file is relevant |
| `@folder <path>/` | Folder context | All files in directory | When majority of files are relevant |
| `@code <symbol>` | Surgical context | Specific symbol | Function, class, variable, constant |
| `@rule-name.mdc` | Rule context | Specific rule file | Load project guidance rules |

### Reference Examples

```markdown
@src/components/UserProfile.tsx                    # Single file
@frontend/                                          # All files in frontend/
@LRUCachedFunction                                  # Specific function
@UserInterface                                      # Specific class/interface
@MAX_RETRY_COUNT                                    # Specific constant
@init.mdc                                           # Specific rule
```

---

## Context Efficiency Principle

**Specificity over breadth** -- Provide just enough context to prevent hallucinations without overwhelming the agent.

### Hierarchy of Context Precision

| Precision | Syntax | Token Cost | Recommendation |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Surgical** | `@code <symbol>` | Lowest | **Preferred** -- minimal tokens, maximum relevance |
| **File** | `@file <path>` | Medium | Use for small, focused files |
| **Folder** | `@folder <path>/` | High | Use only when most files in folder are relevant |
| **Broad** | `@folder/**/*.ext` | Highest | Avoid unless necessary |

### Decision Matrix

| Task | Recommended Reference | Why |
|---|---|---|
| "How does this function work?" | `@code functionName` | Only the function matters |
| "Review this file" | `@file filename.ext` | Whole file is relevant |
| "Refactor this module" | `@folder module/` | Many files interact |
| "Add feature across project" | Multiple `@file` references | Only specific files matter |

