## Key Textual Documentation

Maintain key textual documentation in the repo so Cursor can ingest it as context:

### Essential Documentation Files

| File | Purpose | When Referenced |
|---|---|---|
| `README.md` | Project overview | Onboarding, architecture questions |
| `docs/api.md` | API specifications | API implementation, integration |
| `docs/design-docs/` | Architecture decisions | System design questions |
| `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` | AI guidance | All interactions (if alwaysApply) |
| `CONTRIBUTING.md` | Team workflows | Onboarding, process questions |

### Best Practices

- Keep documentation **version-controlled** and **synchronized with code**
- Use **semantic conventions**: expand acronyms on first use, include links to related standards
- Include **Mermaid or PlantUML diagrams** for architecture visualization
- Generate documentation **automatically in CI/CD** to keep it current

